---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const CALENDLY = 'https://calendly.com/russell-decisive/30min';

const title = 'Finance for the trades | Decisive';
const description =
  'Your crews earn the margin. Your numbers can\'t prove it. Job costs, WIP, and bid pricing read in dollars, in 14 days, on guarantee.';

const traps = [
  {
    name: 'Anchoring',
    body: 'Bids priced to costs that moved two years ago are margin you gave away before the crew ever rolled. Anchored bid pricing is the most common trapped margin in the trades, job by job.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Status Quo',
    body: 'Sub invoices and material receipts that never land on the job that spent them mean the true cost of a job shows up 60 days after closeout, long after the next bid went out on the same bad math.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Loss Aversion',
    body: 'The general contractor account you are most afraid to reprice is often the one capping your margin. The math never gets run because losing the relationship feels worse than the leak.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">For owner-led trades: construction, HVAC, electrical, plumbing</span>
      <h1>
        <span class="h1-line">Your crews earn the margin.</span>
        <span class="h1-line h1-line-accent">Your numbers can't prove it.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-subhead">
        Job costs that land late, WIP nobody trusts, and bids priced to stale costs hide which jobs actually make money. <span class="dollar">We price the answer in dollars.</span> Guaranteed 3x your Diagnostic fee in recoverable value, in 14 days.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={CALENDLY}>Book a fit call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">See the 14-day Diagnostic</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-microcopy">30 minutes with Russ. No pitch. You leave knowing where to look first.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Where the margin hides in the trades</span>
        <h2>The margin is earned on the job. It disappears in the books.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          WIP accuracy, over and under-billing, retainage, job costs that land on the job that spent them, and which GC relationships actually pay: the numbers that decide what to bid next. Most contractors bid this week on last quarter's math.
        </p>
        <div class="category-pull">
          Your books tell you what happened. They can't tell you what to do next.
        </div>
        <p>
          The decisions weren't wrong. You made them on the only numbers you had, and those numbers were never built to decide from. Everyone who touches your books is paid to serve something else: the filing, the close, the report. Nobody is paid to make the next call defensible, and that is the job we do.
        </p>
        <div class="delay-callout">
          We don't audit the past. We make the next call defensible.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="traps">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Where the value is trapped</div>
      <h2>Three traps that eat a contractor's margin.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.88);">
        The Six Trap Diagnostic&trade; reads your numbers through the decisions that produced them. Three of the six do the most damage in the trades. The patterns are structural, not failures of the owner.
      </p>
      <div class="trap-grid">
        {traps.map((t, i) => (
          <div class="trap-card">
            <div class="trap-num">Trap {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
            <div class="trap-name">{t.name}</div>
            <p>{t.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="traps-footer">
        We name the stack, price each one in dollars, and turn the read into a plan. We don't audit the past. We make the next call defensible.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Proof</span>
        <h2>The mechanism reads the same across industries, because the traps do.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="worked">
        <span class="label">Manufacturer, $15M revenue</span>
        <h4>The account nobody would touch was the margin everyone was looking for.</h4>
        <p>
          The biggest account felt untouchable, so the math never got run. Full cost allocation showed it was funded by everyone else. We repriced and reset terms instead of protecting the logo. The same pattern lives in a contractor's largest GC relationship.
        </p>
        <div class="calc">
          <div><span class="k">Least profitable account</span><span class="v accent">The largest one</span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Margins moved</span><span class="v">15% to 22%</span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Time to recover</span><span class="v">90 days</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 22px;">
        Anonymized by segment and revenue band until attribution is confirmed. Trades outcomes available in conversation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Tiers and pricing</span>
        <h2>Find. Install. Run.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Most owners start with the 14-day Decision Diagnostic and move into the 90-Day Resolution. Pricing is banded by revenue, and the floor is $5M.
        </p>
        <p class="promise-line">
          The Diagnostic promise: at least 3x the fee in owner-accepted value identified by Day 14, or you pay nothing.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta-row" style="margin-top: 8px;">
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/#tiers">See tiers and pricing</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/guarantee">Read the guarantee</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="close-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Book a fit call</span>
      <h2>Decide from the numbers. Prove it in the cash.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        In 14 days you know what your money is actually doing, in dollars: the traps that are running, the recoverable value, and the first three moves, whether or not we ever work together again. It starts with one 30-minute call.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={CALENDLY}>Book a fit call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">See the 14-day Diagnostic</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero-microcopy { font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7); margin: 10px 0 0; }
  .promise-line { font-family: Inter, sans-serif; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin-top: 8px; }
</style>
